        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>errorIfDisabled</name>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Controls behavior of a tool when disabled. If true (the default) and a tool&apos;s primary feature set is disabled (such as when ROSE is compiled with too old a compiler or without the necessary supporting software packages), then the tool should emit an error message and exit with a failure status. When this data member is false, then the tool will silently exit with success, which is useful during &quot;make check&quot; or similar testing. </para>        </detaileddescription>
